original_story.7:
Access to Health Care Services
Access to healthcare services is a critical issue impacting the well-being of communities, and assessing how residents in San Francisco utilize these services provides vital insights. This data story delves into trends regarding medical care access, particularly focusing on the percentage of residents who reported delaying medical care between 2007 and 2016. Additionally, it examines the health coverage for children in the Child Care Health Program, highlighting the percentage of children with current physical exams from 2012 to 2017. Furthermore, transit service scores for public health facilities are analyzed to understand how transportation influences access to healthcare. Lastly, the ethnic match between residents and physicians is scrutinized, showcasing the demographics of both groups in 2013. Each of these aspects contributes to a broader understanding of the accessibility and provision of health services in the area.
