This data-driven story provides an in-depth analysis of flight performance within the airline industry, focusing on the proportions of on-time arrivals, delays, cancellations, and diversions. Overall, approximately 78.9% of all flights arrive on time, with the remaining percentages allocated to varied circumstances such as delays (19.1%), cancellations (1.7%), and diversions (0.3%). The trend over time indicates significant fluctuations in flight numbers, especially during peak seasonal periods, maintaining an upward trajectory in overall flight counts since 2017. The analysis further explores the correlation between factors affecting delays, highlighting that the majority are attributable to internal airline operations and late aircraft arrivals, with minimal impact from weather or security issues. Key visualizations include pie charts reflecting arrival proportions, area charts detailing flight statistics over time, and bar charts representing individual carrier performance, providing a comprehensive perspective on the factors influencing airline efficiency.
Average Arrival Proportion
