CO2 emission story
The CO2 emission story explores the critical issue of carbon emissions worldwide, shedding light on the principal contributors to atmospheric CO2. By analyzing data on emissions from countries, continents, and specific industrial activities, this narrative aims to illustrate the scope of the problem, pinpoint the major offenders, and highlight trends over time. Key insights reveal that the United States and China are at the forefront of global emissions, while various countries and continents contribute differently to the pollution matrix. Detailed breakdowns also reveal the underlying causes of emissions in specific contexts, such as India's reliance on coal and oil. The following visualizations provide an in-depth perspective on these global challenges and foster understanding of the urgent need for impactful climate action.
