original_story.21:
2022 RI PIT Storybook Homelessness
The 2022 RI PIT Storybook provides an insightful examination of homelessness trends in Rhode Island over the past five years, highlighting critical shifts across various settings and demographics. The data underscores a significant increase in the overall homeless population, which has risen by 10% since 2018. Notably, emergency shelters and unsheltered individuals have contributed to this uptick, despite a decline in transitional housing options. Families experiencing homelessness have faced reductions largely due to the closure of transitional housing programs. Among youth aged 18-24, the number of unaccompanied individuals in shelters has also increased, underscoring the growing need for targeted services. Furthermore, an equity analysis reveals stark racial disparities in homelessness, emphasizing the disproportionate impact on certain communities.
