Story Heating fuel trends
The trends in heating fuel usage show a significant evolution over the decades, particularly in Maine. The graphs illustrate how the reliance on fuel oil for heating rose consistently until the year 2000, peaking substantially in the 1960s. As preferences shifted, the use of natural gas and electricity grew, particularly in the late 20th and early 21st centuries. Observations include a notable crossover in the 1980s, where electric heating overtook fuel oil in popularity. The projected rise in natural gas prices also suggests a potential turning point for heating fuel dynamics, particularly as more households consider alternative heating options.
