original_story.25:
Unemployment and Community College Enrollment Story
This data story explores the intricate relationship between unemployment rates and community college enrollment trends in the United States, particularly before and during the COVID-19 pandemic. Historically, community college enrollment has shown a consistent pattern of increase or decrease in tandem with changes in unemployment rates. The analysis focuses on data from the 1980s through the early 2000s, highlighting significant shifts, especially during periods of economic downturn. In 2020, the COVID crisis disrupted these patterns, signaling an unprecedented divergence between enrollment and unemployment trends. Additionally, we investigate state-level variations, with a spotlight on Oregon, illustrating how local circumstances can influence broader national trends. Through visualizations, we will examine these dynamics and draw insights into how economic conditions shape educational pursuits within communities.
