University of West Georgia SACSCOC Peer Institutions Benchmark Report
The University of West Georgia's SACSCOC Peer Institutions Benchmark Report offers a comprehensive analysis of key performance indicators related to student enrollment, graduation rates, and retention rates among peer institutions in the Southern region. By evaluating the Full-Time Equivalent (FTE) enrollment from Fall 2018 and comparing it with peers such as West Florida, Valdosta State, and Kennesaw State, useful insights into the university's positioning can be drawn. The analysis extends into graduation rates, highlighting 4-year outcomes alongside demographic factors that reveal disparities among student cohorts. The retention rates provide another layer of context to the university's performance, illustrating the continuity of student engagement. Furthermore, an overview of the ethnic composition of the student population aligns this data with diversity metrics across comparable institutions. Overall, this report serves as a valuable resource for evaluating the University of West Georgia's metrics relative to its peers, informing strategic planning and initiatives for improvement.
