Beaver Education - Population Story
The Beaver Education - Population Story explores the demographic shifts within Beaver County, focusing on the correlation between population changes and school enrollment trends over the decades. From 1970 to 2030, Beaver County anticipates a significant decrease in population, with more than 48,000 residents lost. This shrinking population will inevitably affect the school-age cohort, projected to decline by around 34,000 children, excluding those under five. The implications are stark, as the county is expected to witness a drastic drop of approximately 32,500 enrolled students compared to 1970 numbers. Through detailed visualizations, we will analyze historical enrollment data across various districts and evaluate how changes in the total population correspond with school-age demographics and enrollment figures.
