Buckinghamshire's labor productivity story
Buckinghamshire's labor productivity story reveals a complex landscape of economic performance relative to national benchmarks. As the data illustrates, Buckinghamshire ranks as the 9th highest in productivity among 38 Local Enterprise Partnership (LEP) areas, just shy of the UK average. However, it also underscores the disparities within the Oxford-Cambridge Arc, highlighting significant variations in productivity across local authorities. While Buckinghamshire boasts a solid productivity index, trends over the past decade reveal a steady decline since 2010, indicating challenges ahead. The region faced a notable slowdown in productivity growth from 2014 to 2018, further complicating its economic narrative. Additionally, when factoring out rental income, Buckinghamshire’s productivity drops significantly, altering its relative position among LEPs. This story is important as it reflects the interplay between industrial dynamics, economic policy, and local realities in shaping Buckinghamshire's economic outlook.
