  }
}
</visualization>
Possible Benefit of Early Childhood Education
WV has received higher ratings than KY for early childhood education. OK has been noted as one of the first states with universal preschool for 4-year-olds and high attendance rates. WV, KY and OK have similar demographics: black populations below 10% and poverty rates in black and white families above the national average. The preschool poverty gap, defined as the difference in preschool attendance rates of children who do or do not live in poverty, was substantially lower in WV (4.6 percentage points) than in Kentucky (15.6) in 2014. This may partially explain why Kentucky's black students showed less improvement over time than West Virginia's."
