Possible Benefit of Policies Reducing Lead Exposure from Old Homes
Lead exposure from living in old homes is strongly associated with reduced academic performance; Rhode Island illustrates that lead exposure reduction can narrow the racial achievement gap. Rhode Island's black students performed well below the national average in 1990 but experienced improvements similar to those in NY, NJ and CT, ending up just slightly below the national average in 2015. Rhode Island's white students improved at a similar rate as those in NJ and MA, the two highest-performing groups in the region"
